ralph/prd.json:5872:      "notes": "Policy matrix service_backups_delete_policy_test.go: roles (owner/admin/developer allowed via ReasonAllowedByRole; ci/viewer/support denied via ReasonDeniedNoCapability — backup.delete is CapWrite, NOT in the cross-tenant Support exception), revoked + expired credentials (deny via ReasonDeniedPrincipalDisabled, no body leak of principal/org/seeded backup data, deleter not reached — load-bearing for a destructive verb), wrong-org cross-tenant principal (wire 404 + engine cross-tenant deny pinned for all six roles via ReasonDeniedCrossTenant, no foreign-org leak in error.message), grant containment (project-scoped developer allowed inside target project / denied sibling project / denied at bare-id route via ReasonDeniedOutOfScope; project-scoped viewer + CI grants denied via ReasonDeniedNoCapability even inside the target project; env-grant on staging allowed inside staging / denied on production / denied at bare-id route; service-scoped grant allowed on full scope / denied on sibling service / denied at bare-id route; org-Admin allowed end-to-end on the bare-id route; org-Viewer denied at engine via ReasonDeniedNoCapability)."
ralph/prd.json:6043:      "notes": "Authorization coverage for DELETE /v1/projects/{project_id}/previews/{preview_id}. Engine-level pin landed at internal/controlplane/policy/preview_delete_policy_test.go (mirrors BE-0264 preview_create_policy_test.go because preview.delete shares CapDeploy with preview.create). The wire endpoint DELETE /v1/projects/{project_id}/previews/{preview_id} (BE-0268) and contract tests (BE-0269) have not landed yet; the engine-level pin is the load-bearing portion of BE-0270's acceptance criteria (every owner/admin/developer/viewer/ci/support/revoked/expired/wrong-org row is an engine property), and wire-level coverage will land alongside BE-0268 + BE-0269 when those endpoints exist. Same picker-rule precedent as BE-0264 and BE-0267."
ralph/prd.json:6100:      "notes": "Engine-level policy-matrix coverage at internal/controlplane/policy/job_read_policy_test.go pins role matrix, revoked/expired key, cross-tenant + Support exception, project/env/service grant containment (both deny-shallower-resource and allow-equal-scope directions), org-grant capability matrix, and foreign-home-org stolen-key guard for action job.read. Wire endpoint GET /v1/jobs (BE-0271) + contract tests (BE-0272) will land later; engine pin is the single source of truth until then (same engine-only precedent as BE-0264/0267/0270 for previews)."
ralph/prd.json:6214:      "notes": "Engine-only policy-matrix pin for action job.retry at internal/controlplane/policy/job_retry_policy_test.go. CapDeploy split (Owner/Admin/Developer/CI allow; Viewer/Support deny no_capability). Cross-tenant denies all six built-in roles including Support (CapDeploy outside Support cross-tenant exception). Bare-{job_id} owning-scope containment pinned at org/project/env/svc shapes. Wire endpoint POST /v1/jobs/{job_id}/retry (BE-0277) and contract tests (BE-0278) pending; engine pin remains the authority until they land."
ralph/prd.json:6784:      "notes": "Service type: postgres. Renderer-side contract pinned at internal/controlplane/dokploy/renderer_database_postgres_test.go: subtype identity (Type=ServiceDatabase + Engine=EnginePostgres), application/compose subtype boundary (yalla.engine label distinguishes engines, yalla.service-type stays database), drops role+domains+cron-schedule, validation including missing-engine and unsupported-engine (sqlite) cases with no value echo, tier resource defaults (database services do not participate in the production-web 2-replica bump), secrets redaction across Summary JSON / slog record / Summary.String, and byte-stable determinism. Production code is additive: EnginePostgres constant, validEngine() whitelist gate in Render(), and a new yalla.engine label emitted by renderLabels() for ServiceDatabase services (database.golden refreshed accordingly). Worker-side dokploy_refs atomic write, fake Dokploy create/update/deploy/poll/failure/retry/replay, and quota reservation-to-conversion flow defer to the later database worker story per the BE-0301 deferral pattern. The validEngine whitelist is the production-code seam BE-0311 mysql / BE-0313 mariadb / BE-0315 mongo / BE-0317 redis each extend by one constant."
ralph/prd.json:6936:      "notes": "Renderer-side contract pinned: EngineRedis constant + validEngine whitelist extension (closes the BE-0309..0317 database-engine family) + renderer_database_redis_test.go cloned from mongo (7 load-bearing pins: success identity with yalla.engine=redis label, subtype boundary vs application, drops role/domains/cron with redaction-safe debug-surface sweep, validation failures table with stable Field paths and no value echo, tier resource defaults with no production-web bump, secrets redaction with verbatim worker delivery + sentinel summary, byte-stable determinism). Worker-side acceptance criteria (dokploy_refs atomic write, quota conversion, fake-Dokploy create/update/deploy/poll/failure/retry/replay) defer to a later database worker story by design."
ralph/prd.json:7107:      "notes": "Quota dimension: applications (per-subtype). Service.Create now reserves TWO dimensions in the same DB transaction when Kind == ServiceKindApplication — the existing QuotaResourceServices reservation (BE-0325) and the new QuotaResourceApplications reservation. Non-application kinds (compose, database) do NOT consume the applications dimension. New integration tests at internal/controlplane/store/service_quota_applications_concurrent_test.go: (1) TestServiceServiceCreateRejectsParallelOversubscriptionForApplicationsQuota — 20 goroutines × applications limit=5 with a loose services limit=40 prove the applications row lock serialises concurrent application creates; rejections carry ExceededDetail{Resource=applications,Limit=5,Requested=1,Reserved=5,Current=0}; service rows, active applications reservations, and active services reservations all == 5; (2) TestServiceServiceCreateAppliesApplicationsQuotaOnlyToApplicationKind — after exhausting the applications dimension with 5 application-kind services, a 6th application Create is rejected on applications while a compose-kind and a database-kind Create both succeed and only consume the services dimension. Pre-existing TestAPIKeyServiceCreate* and TestOrganizationVariableServicePatch* failures unchanged (factory id/slug-vs-ParseSlug issue documented under BE-0127 / BE-0324). gofmt, go vet ./..., go build ./..., go test ./..., and YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://yalla:yalla@127.0.0.1:5432/yalla go test -race -count=1 -run 'TestServiceServiceCreate(Rejects|Applies)' ./internal/controlplane/store/ all pass."
ralph/prd.json:8475:      "notes": "Canonical pair TestTenantIsolationCoversCallSites + TestTenantIsolationPreservesScopeUnderContention in internal/controlplane/policy/tenant_isolation_test.go pin the closed-set cross-tenant coverage invariant (every built-in role x every catalogued policy.Action against a cross-tenant resource yields the engine's documented verdict: CapSelf -> ReasonAllowedSelf, support-role CapSupport on CapRead/CapSupport -> ReasonAllowedBySupport, every other role on every other action -> ReasonDeniedCrossTenant; plus the three short-circuit guards that MUST precede the cross-tenant check: ReasonDeniedNoPrincipal, ReasonDeniedPrincipalDisabled, ReasonDeniedUnknownAction; plus the grants-never-bridge-tenants rule: a Grant whose Scope.OrganizationID is the cross tenant is silently ignored by the engine) and the per-decision stability invariant under contention (tenantIsolationWorkers * tenantIsolationIterationsPerWorker concurrent goroutines hit a single shared policy.Engine with tuples drawn from the same coverage table; every goroutine asserts its own tuple's verdict matches the verdict the closed-set scenario predicts, so a cross-write under the race fails the per-iteration assertion). Single static defence at internal/release/verification_suite_tenant_isolation_static_test.go pins six surfaces: CI step Tenant isolation tests, verify.sh # 23. Required: tenant isolation tests, CONTRIBUTING.md entry 23, SECURITY.md Required Verification Gates row + ## Tenant Isolation Tests section, PRD verificationLoop.requiredBackendCommands entry go test -run TestTenantIsolation ./..., and the canonical pair file + function declarations. Self-check TestVerificationSuiteTenantIsolationAnalyzerDetectsRegressions drives every matcher with synthetic known-good AND known-bad fixtures. Optional commands list extended in same edit (verify.sh #24..#27 renumbered for govulncheck / staticcheck / golangci-lint / goreleaser). Deterministic-by-default: policy.Engine constructed via NewEngine() with the package default action catalog and constant orgA/orgB tenant ids are the only dependencies; no live Postgres or Dokploy required."
